  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Undra Firdosh Arifbhai vs Chief Officer, Dahod Nagar Palika on 26 March, 2024 Author: Vaibhavi D. Nanavati Bench: Vaibhavi D. Nanavati Neutral C/Sca/21494/2023 Order",
    "facts": "It is the case of the writ-applicant that by way of present writ-application the writ-applicant herein seeks direction to provide legal and valid NOC and permission for running slaughter house under the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 for licensing and registration of food business.",
    "arguments": "5. Mr. Bloch, the learned advocate appearing for the writ- applicant on instructions states that the writ-applicant would prefer an application in the prescribed format with the respondent authority and that the same be decided by the respondent authority in terms of the order passed by the Hon'ble Division Bench in the Civil Application No.10 of 2023 in Writ Petition (PIL) No.133 of 2021 dated 11.4.2023 in paragraphs 6.3 and 6.4. 6. Considering the aforesaid and statement made by Mr. Bloch, the learned advocate appearing for the writ-applicant, if the writ-applicant were to approach the respondent authority by preferring an application in the prescribed format seeking permission to run a slaughter house, the same be considered by the respondent authority in accordance with law and in line with the ratio laid down in order dated 11.4.2023 passed in NEUTRAL CITATION C/SCA/21494/2023 ORDER DATED: 26/03/2024 undefined the Civil Application No.10 of 2023 in Writ Petition (PIL) No.133 of 2021.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. Mr. Bloch, the learned advocate appearing for the writ- applicant on instructions states that the writ-applicant would prefer an application in the prescribed format with the respondent authority and that the same be decided by the respondent authority in terms of the order passed by the Hon'ble Division Bench in the Civil Application No.10 of 2023 in Writ Petition (PIL) No.133 of 2021 dated 11.4.2023 in paragraphs 6.3 and 6.4. 6. Considering the aforesaid and statement made by Mr. Bloch, the learned advocate appearing for the writ-applicant, if the writ-applicant were to approach the respondent authority by preferring an application in the prescribed format seeking permission to run a slaughter house, the same be considered by the respondent authority in accordance with law and in line with the ratio laid down in order dated 11.4.2023 passed in NEUTRAL CITATION C/SCA/21494/2023 ORDER DATED: 26/03/2024 undefined the Civil Application No.10 of 2023 in Writ Petition (PIL) No.133 of 2021.",
